cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this simulation study, please cite it as below."
title: "Bubble-Tea Shop Simulation: Is Fast-Item Triage Worth It?"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "dwan621"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dwan621/bubble-tea-shop-sim"
license: MIT
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-16"
abstract: >-
  Discrete-event simulation study of a bubble-tea shop with a shared clerk pool
  selling tea, bread and ice cream. It compares synchronised vs split delivery
  for mixed tea + ice-cream orders, fast-item priority, and the economics of
  waiting, with break-even and sensitivity analyses.
keywords:
  - discrete-event simulation
  - queueing
  - operations management
  - priority scheduling
  - service operations
